Merge with two indexes into a new slice, then copy back:
```go
out := make([]T, 0, len(s))
i, j := 0, mid
for i < mid && j < len(s) {
	if cmp(s[j], s[i]) < 0 {
		out = append(out, s[j]); j++
	} else {
		out = append(out, s[i]); i++
	}
}
out = append(out, s[i:mid]...)
out = append(out, s[j:]...)
copy(s, out)
```
In the solution file the parameter `cmp` hides the `cmp` package inside `SortFunc`; that's fine, `Sort` still sees it and passes `cmp.Compare[T]`.
